\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Joint posteriors on the foreground-contaminated synthetic sky, marginalising over the three free template amplitudes of Eq.~\eqref  {eq:fg_model} with $\mathcal  {N}(1, 0.5)$ priors. The joint gains persist, but the CNC-induced $\Omega _{\mathrm  {m}}$ offset now propagates into the combination and is absorbed by the most tSZ-degenerate template amplitude, $A_{\mathrm  {IR}}$, which is biased by $+3.8\sigma $.}}{5}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:syn_fg}{{6}{5}{Joint posteriors on the foreground-contaminated synthetic sky, marginalising over the three free template amplitudes of Eq.~\eqref {eq:fg_model} with $\mathcal {N}(1, 0.5)$ priors. The joint gains persist, but the CNC-induced $\Omega _{\mathrm {m}}$ offset now propagates into the combination and is absorbed by the most tSZ-degenerate template amplitude, $A_{\mathrm {IR}}$, which is biased by $+3.8\sigma $}{figure.6}{}}
